<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.10.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01911</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.10.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>be28cce2-9b41-4f5a-a8aa-9a9f17386fe1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_262d2f52-e31f-47b2-b66a-60f84a626b00" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002">A quadratic function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">Without graphing, identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00009">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (0,10), which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is -3, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (-10,0), which is 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.1 – 7.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>\</m:mi><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mi>d</m:mi><m:mi>\</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 7, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives 0 10, which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is -3, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives -10 0, which is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f0164bac-d1a1-4b0c-b157-a5fc12ce0d62" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00012">Use the standard form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> to identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00013">Correct! – 21 The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph of the equation is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.1 – 7.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">The correct answer is – 21. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph of the equation is (0,-21).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_55ce37f4-0387-4fe9-b5ef-28c37e3645c7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00016">Answer these questions for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of this equation’s graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00018">Correct! 4 The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph of the equation is (0,4).</para>
            <para id="para-00019">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.2 and 7.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00020">The correct answer is 4. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph of the equation is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_68bfe074-e46a-4486-b055-66aa9b00bc06" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00021">An equivalent way to write this equation is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. What are the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of this equation’s graph?</para>
            <para id="para-00022">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00023"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00024"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00025"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00026"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00027">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> . If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 4, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> which is 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.2 and 7.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 4, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> which is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4d4d9630-91aa-4245-94f5-1a8c6d8fab42" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00030">Noah said that if we graph <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts will be at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Is Noah correct?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00031">Correct! We can check by substituting 1 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and -6 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and see if they produce an output of 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (0)(7), which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is – 6, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (-7)(0), which is 0.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.2 – 7.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00033">The correct answer is Yes. We can check by substituting 1 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and – 6 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and see if they produce an output of 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 1, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (0)(7), which is 0. If <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is – 6, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> gives (-7)(0), which is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f272ae94-b434-4557-98ef-c4fcb2d3a5a9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00034"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of this graph.
          
          (<media alt="A curve in an x y plane, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 6, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 8 to 8, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 1 comma 0, 1 comma negative 4, and 3 comma 0."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_12_10_01.svg"/></media>)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00035">Correct! The graph crosses the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">Try again. Revisit activities 7.10.2 and 7.10.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00037">The correct answer is – 1 and 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_3477c014-4164-47c2-a96d-60d6aefb0a20" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            
            <para id="para-00038">Use the standard form of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> to identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            
            <para id="para-00039">Try again. Revisit activity 7.10.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00040">The correct answer is 8.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
